# === MedNorm-VI .gitignore ===
# Keep base models, adapters, raw competition data, generated indices, and
# prediction outputs OUT of version control. Only code, configs, docs, tests,
# and small tracked fixtures belong in the repository.

# --- Local Vietnamese architecture specification (authoritative doc is the
#     English PDF; the Vietnamese copy is intentionally untracked) ---
MedNorm-VI_Architecture_Vietnamese.pdf

# --- Model weights / checkpoints / adapters ---
# Operator-selected LOCAL checkpoint store. Never committed, never pushed, never
# Git LFS. The global *.pt rule below already covers the bytes; these two
# repository-root rules make the intent explicit and also catch a checkpoint
# dropped at the root by hand.
runs/
/checkpoint/
/best.pt

models/**
!models/.gitkeep
!models/README.md
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.gguf
*.onnx

# Phase-2 Colab/operator artifact roots. Notebooks write these to Drive by
# default, but local dry-runs must also stay out of Git.
artifacts/**
!artifacts/.gitkeep
weights/**
# Repository-root caches directory (pip/HF/torchinductor). The `/`-anchored rule
# ignores the DIRECTORY itself, not only its contents, so `git status` cannot show
# it as untracked and `git add -A` cannot pick up a partially matched path.
# Audit 0051 deleted 1,075,833,774 bytes of reproducible cache from here.
/caches/
caches/**

# --- Raw / private competition data & KB snapshots ---
# Namespaced by trust level. Organizer test inputs are INPUT ONLY and never
# labeled. Only READMEs and .gitkeep markers are tracked; real data stays out.
data/**
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/**/README.md
# Phase 1C-A resource governance: re-include ONLY these directories so git
# descends into them (git will not apply a nested file exception if the parent
# dir is treated as excluded). Other data/ subdirs keep their prior behavior.
!data/external/
!data/external/**/
!data/derived/
!data/manifests/
# Filled-in resource/KB governance manifests (metadata only) ARE tracked; the raw
# RxNorm/ICD/NER payloads they describe stay ignored above.
!data/manifests/*.yaml
!data/manifests/*.yml
# Public NER corpora may be acquired locally for review, but raw payloads and
# nested downloaded repositories remain untracked.
data/external/public_ner/**

# --- Generated evaluation / experiment reports ---
reports/**
!reports/.gitkeep
!reports/README.md

# --- Experiment registry: EXP-*.json records ARE tracked (diff-friendly);
#     only generated outputs/predictions are ignored elsewhere. ---

# --- Generated retrieval indices ---
indices/**
!indices/.gitkeep
!indices/README.md

# --- Prediction outputs & submission packages ---
outputs/**
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/README.md
outputs/
output/
*.zip

# Operator-placed LOCAL copies of Colab training artifacts. Audit 0036 already
# ignores artifacts/, weights/ and caches/; this covers the local-artifacts/
# convention observed during Audit 0042. Generated training output is never
# committed.
local-artifacts/

# --- Audit run artifacts (numbered audit .md files under docs/audits/ ARE tracked) ---
docs/audits/**/*.log
docs/audits/**/*.json

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
credentials*.json

# --- AI-assistant local files (never commit; kept locally under .claude/) ---
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.md
.claude/
.claude.json

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
